This product can download and run OpenCode (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode,
also published as npm package opencode-ai and Homebrew formula anomalyco/tap/opencode),
Copyright (c) AnomalyCo / SST contributors, used under the MIT License. OpenCode is not
vendored in this repository; Hypurr installs a pinned release binary into
~/.hypurr/agents/opencode with the user's consent. Free Zen models (Big Pickle and
others) are provided by OpenCode for a limited time under OpenCode's Zen terms; some
free models may use prompts to improve the model. See https://opencode.ai/docs/zen/.

---

Android terminal (phone project shell) vendors the Apache-2.0 `terminal-emulator`
and `terminal-view` libraries from Termux (https://github.com/termux/termux-app,
tag v0.118.0), originally from jackpal Android Terminal Emulator
(https://github.com/jackpal/Android-Terminal-Emulator). See
apps/android/terminal-emulator/LICENSE and apps/android/terminal-view/LICENSE.
Hypurr does not include Termux app code (GPLv3). Local JNI PTY support was removed;
the session bridges to the host openShell PTY over the existing channel.
